## Start here

{% if claude_terminal == 'started' %}
- The terminal below runs Claude Code: `claude --continue` picks this folder's conversation up; `/clear` starts afresh.
{% elif claude_terminal == 'listed' and code_claude_task_there | default(false) | bool %}
- In the window of `{{ again }}`, the task **Claude (just code)** runs Claude Code in a terminal of {{ editor_name }}'s, which is this VM's: it picks the folder's conversation up, or starts a fresh one where a `claude` already has it open; `/clear` starts afresh. In any other window, run `claude` in its terminal. How to start the task: `docs/guides/{{ code_editor }}.md` in the project.
{% else %}
- Run `claude` in {{ editor_name }}'s terminal, which is this VM's: `claude --continue` picks the folder's conversation up; `/clear` starts afresh.
{% endif %}
- Your repositories are in `{{ code_root }}`: `cd {{ code_root }}/<repo>`.
- `gh pr create` and `gh pr checks` work once `gh` is signed in.
- Docker runs without sudo: `docker ps`.

## From your machine

| Command | Does |
|---|---|
| `{{ again }}` | open this window again |
| `just login {{ name }} --only claude{{ on }}` | sign Claude Code in |
{% if github_auth | default(true) | bool %}
| `just login {{ name }} --only github{{ on }}` | sign `gh` in, then clone the private repositories |
{% endif %}
{% if tailscale_wanted | default(tailscale_enabled | default(true)) | bool %}
| `just login {{ name }} --only tailscale{{ on }}` | sign it in to Tailscale |
{% endif %}
| `just deploy {{ name }} --only configure{{ on }}` | run the configuration again; `--tags <role>` for one part of it |
| `just status` · `just logs` | the fleet, and what it needs · the run logs |
| `just destroy {{ name }}{{ on }}` | sign it out of everything, then delete it |

