## When something is off

{% if window_tasks %}
- **No Claude terminal, and no notes?** Trust the window (the Restricted Mode banner, Manage, Trust), then allow automatic tasks ("Tasks: Manage Automatic Tasks"), or run "Tasks: Run Task", Claude.
- **Signed in is stale?** "Tasks: Run Task", **Session notes** refreshes it.
- **VS Code asked whether to open this file?** In a one-project window it lies outside the window's folder. Open is remembered for that window; trusting the window of `{{ again }}` once avoids the question in every project's.
{% endif %}
- **"REMOTE HOST IDENTIFICATION HAS CHANGED"** after a rebuild: `ssh-keygen -R {{ vm.address }}` on your machine.
{% if claude_code_remote_control | default(true) | bool %}
- **Not in the Claude apps?** `systemctl status {{ code_remote_control_unit }}` here, then `just deploy {{ name }} --tags claude_code{{ on }}` on your machine.
{% endif %}
- **Private repositories missing?** `just deploy {{ name }} --tags github_projects{{ on }}` on your machine.

## About this file

Written by `just code` and `just deploy` into `{{ code_notes_dir }}`{% if window_tasks %}; its "Signed in" section is rewritten by the window's **Session notes** task each time the window opens{% endif %}. Delete it any time; `editor_session_notes: false` in your inventory stops it.
